ad61b7203ce600\", \"dea065f91186cdabfc0a02a16bca4ee50bb750128390207bf2833baea936585b\", \"7f7ef22f005dba6bb077ac33f519833639971a5f414d83a202e2cc97c15cb539\", \"4cd2f815d16f0b94c2fb2339427d65fef3a83122a55a3487589d5171389ad2fb\", \"0c473b2461e0d45fe1ff41e973cf8adeedb28a0f19a14b8df99e1ddc468bf69d\", \"d14f70288a77ea3ad86cd790291f75f234511f7a024b90eed9c7dbe22284d7cc\", \"8e0ab70e21a2ed9c13b5eb987a1a9b9df0c72edbe2d267e8dd3e9a49d4ef4bd7\", \"1aec7237a9bacdbaedd9318145b3894f6c7a0dc303bea61ad50bfa238fcc0b69\", \"e217ad3a30563c5d1c14ee86b4b7fcca5a6a143141634fe41838a6d06897d145\", \"14875014e3378dd9ec3194dbb350eb8b05f09eaf0cd1710262e258c04bf40006\", \"5cf04447f6d8a27ad3681a0cba759c0f77134aa1bf4024f26a4e92e943607bbc\", \"e90705523609677dfe743cbf0492701f919a4923603c0c1dddb70d9e1b2f0680\", \"5e824d3fb1cd38e34332e0e13dad5a1317a0a0d1b3fa47b549ba81d640927deb\", \"e216d02e58570192eca08e1ba31e96782523d4bd0ed539e56ad52c8dbb1d9c09\", \"8d7a90e2c4e18d643f3e30dad59e2db4b16ada197c0af456255be2ec9c125a77\", \"0dc23471ec00b00b9f6cc176c5294d0c2385cbf154ff0863d605a32464be3b4f\"],\n  \"reviewerType\": \"llm-vision-headless-cli\",\n  \"summary\": \"The five 'narrative' workflows (nomination, selection-publish, vote, meeting-RSVP, discussion-message) carry genuinely good product copy — real titles like 'Parable of the Sower', 'Octavia E. Butler - February reading cycle.', 'Thu, Feb 15 at 7:00 PM - Maya's living room.', 'Closes Jan 20', '10 of 14 spots' — and their action sheets are the strongest screens in the set. Three problems block a pass: the reading-material and shared-library-item workflows are still generic scaffolding ('Task details', 'State saved', 'Reading material opened.', and an ad-network CTA reading 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…' / 'Open ad details' inside a book club), several 'start' captures are scrolled onto the wrong surface entirely (export-metadata start shows the Discussion thread card, meeting-RSVP start shows the AI reading-guide card), and every 'complete' screen prints the same confirmation sentence three times in a row down the page. Layout clipping is pervasive: hero headings are sliced mid-line at the top of six screens and the bottom-nav 'Library' pill runs off the right edge. 12 of 27 screens fail.\",\n  \"holisticQuestionAnswers\": [\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"context-state-legibility\",\n      \"question\": \"Across this community's workflows, is it always clear what workflow and what state (start/in-progress/complete) the user is looking at?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Not consistently. Where the copy is written (nomination, vote, publish, RSVP, discussion) state is very legible without any account concept — the action sheets name themselves in the app bar ('Cast book vote', 'Book meeting RSVP', 'Reply to discussion') and the complete states say 'Vote saved', 'Selection published', 'RSVP confirmed', 'Reply sent'. But three start captures do not show the workflow they claim: 'book-export-metadata_start' shows a purple 'Discussion thread / Prompt: What does community care require?' card with a 'Waiting' chip and no export surface at all, and 'book-meeting-rsvp_start' shows the 'Knowledge and search' / 'Reading guide answer' block with only a clipped 'RSVP to event' button peeking above the fold. The reading-material and library-item workflows are legible as states ('State saved', 'Saved') but not as content — 'Reading material opened.' and 'Shared library custody state updated.' never say which guide or which item.\",\n      \"score\": 52,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"book-export-metadata_start shows 'Discussion thread — Prompt: What does community care require?' with chips 'From Jordan', '3 unread', 'Club scoped' and a 'Waiting' pill; no export card is visible anywhere on the screen\",\n        \"book-meeting-rsvp_start is scrolled to 'Knowledge and search — Cited answers, source visibility, and saved digests.' with the RSVP row sliced to 'Expand | RSVP to event' at the very top edge\",\n        \"book-reading-material_complete states only 'Saved details — Reading material opened.' and repeats 'Reading material opened.' twice more, never naming a guide, chapter, or book\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-meeting-rsvp-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-start\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"copy-accuracy\",\n      \"question\": \"Does displayed text read like real Neighborhood Book Club product copy, or like placeholder scaffolding?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Split down the middle. Real copy exists and is good: 'Parable of the Sower is on the February ballot with title, author, rationale, and meeting context.', 'Focus the chapter 6 discussion on mutual aid, scarcity, and Lauren's journal voice.', 'Checksum BC-042 and export timestamp are written to the owner audit history.', 'Maya's living room', '10 of 14 spots'. Against that, the reading-material and shared-library-item workflows show copy from a different product domain entirely — 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…' with an 'Open ad details' button — plus framework-level headings 'Task details', 'Saved details', 'Activity details', 'Local package details', and chip labels that describe the harness rather than the club: 'Details ready', 'Editable', 'State saved'. Several instructional strings are also visibly internal spec text: 'This view shows editable details, current progress, and the next step before saving.' appears verbatim on eight screens.\",\n      \"score\": 45,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"book-library-item_start and book-reading-material_start both show a card titled 'Reading material' whose body is 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…' with the action 'Open ad details'\",\n        \"book-reading-material_action makes 'Open ad details' the filled primary teal CTA under a heading 'Task details' on a screen whose app bar reads 'Reading material'\",\n        \"The string 'This view shows editable details, current progress, and the next step before saving.' is repeated verbatim on the nomination, vote, RSVP, reading-material and library-item screens\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-action\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-action\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-complete\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"visual-quality\",\n      \"question\": \"Is the visual execution production-grade — no repeated shells, thin content, clipping or crowding?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No. Two systemic defects repeat across the set. First, every 'complete' screen prints its confirmation sentence three times: on book-vote_complete, 'Your vote for Parable of the Sower is confirmed, status is saved, and it can be changed before the ballot closes.' appears as the hero body, again inside 'Vote saved', and again inside 'Vote confirmed' — the same triple-print occurs on the nomination, selection-publish, RSVP, discussion and library complete screens. Second, top-of-frame clipping: book-nomination_start opens on a sliced word 'cycle.', book-vote_start on a half-cut line 'Parable of the Sower is leading the', book-library-item_start on a half-cut 'Members can borrow, queue for, return,'. The bottom navigation's 'Library' pill is cut off by the right screen edge on at least five screens. book-library-item_start also leaves roughly the bottom third of the screen as bare dark-green background under a collapsed 'Local package details' row.\",\n      \"score\": 38,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"book-vote_complete shows the identical sentence 'Your vote for Parable of the Sower is confirmed, status is saved, and it can be changed before the ballot closes.' three times in one scroll\",\n        \"book-nomination_start's first visible text is the sliced descender word 'cycle.' with the line above cut off by the teal app bar\",\n        \"The 'Library' bottom-nav pill is clipped at the right screen edge on book-nomination_start, book-vote_start, book-discussion-message_start and book-meeting-rsvp_start\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-selection-publish-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-meeting-rsvp-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-discussion-message-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-start\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"actionability\",\n      \"question\": \"Are available actions clear, and is it clear why disabled or hidden ones are unavailable?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Partly. Primary CTAs are unambiguous and well labelled — 'Submit nomination', 'Record vote', 'Publish announcement', 'RSVP to event', 'Send message'. Two problems recur. Background cards show a pill literally reading 'Not available' with a slash icon, explained only by 'Another community role manages this item.' — that names no role and offers no path, so the user cannot tell what would unlock it. And every action sheet duplicates its secondary action twice: 'Edit nomination' appears as an outlined button mid-card and again as a dark-green ghost link at the card's bottom-right that renders at very low contrast against the near-black card ('Edit nomination', 'Save draft', 'Change vote', 'Change response', 'Archive thread', 'Edit details' all do this). On book-search-ai-digest_action a card titled 'Answer actions' promises 'Open cited sources, save the answer, refine the query, or share it with members' but renders no buttons at all — only prose bullets.\",\n      \"score\": 55,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"book-vote_start shows two cards whose only action pill is 'Not available' beside the explanation 'Another community role manages this item.' with no role named\",\n        \"book-nomination_action repeats 'Edit nomination' as both an outlined button and a low-contrast green ghost link at the bottom-right of the same card\",\n        \"book-search-ai-digest_action's 'Answer actions' card lists 'Open cited sources, save the answer, refine the query, or share it with members.' but shows no tappable controls\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-action\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-search-ai-digest-action\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-selection-publish-action\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"persona-scoping-correctness\",\n      \"question\": \"Does what each screen shows make sense for the workflow being demonstrated?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Mostly yes for the authored workflows — an organizer-flavoured publish screen ('From organizer', 'Audience: members'), a member-flavoured vote screen ('Your vote will count once for Parable of the Sower'), and an owner-flavoured export screen ('Owner can download the archive after checksum verification succeeds.') are each internally coherent, and the flat-schema absence of a signed-in identity is not a problem. The scoping failures are content ones: an advertising-preferences surface surfaced inside the club's reading-material slot, and two start captures parked on a different workflow's card than the row claims.\",\n      \"score\": 62,\n      \"blocksPass\": false,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"book-selection-publish_action correctly scopes to the organizer with chips 'Audience: members', 'From organizer', 'Today 5:00 PM', 'Inbox + push'\",\n        \"book-export-metadata_action correctly scopes to the owner: 'Member email, phone, and private thread metadata are redacted unless the owner has consent.'\",\n        \"book-reading-material_start places 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…' inside the book club's reading-material surface\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-selection-publish-action\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-action\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-start\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screenReviews\": [\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The purple nomination hero is sliced mid-sentence at the top — the first legible text is the orphan word 'cycle.' — so the screen opens without ever naming the book being nominated, despite the body copy 'Share why this title belongs on the ballot and how it fits the upcoming discussion.' being decent. Below it two identical dark card shells ('Book vote' and 'Shared library item') repeat the same four-control layout ('Tap for expanded view' / 'Member form' / 'Expand' / trailing action), and the second one's trailing action is a disabled 'Not available' pill justified only by 'Another community role manages this item.' The 'Book vote' shell's description is itself truncated placeholder-ish text: 'Member form captures labeled details, privacy c…'. The bottom-nav 'Library' pill is cut off by the right screen edge.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A nomination start card that opens fully in frame naming the title and author being nominated, with the two supporting cards showing real vote/library state rather than duplicated generic shells, and any unavailable action naming the role that owns it.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Orphan clipped word 'cycle.' at top of the purple card\", \"'Book title entered', 'Author confirmed', 'Discussion reason', 'Ballot eligible' chips\", \"'Submit nomination' ghost CTA\", \"'Member form captures labeled details, privacy c…' truncated with ellipsis\", \"'Not available' disabled pill on the Shared library item card\", \"'Library' bottom-nav pill clipped at right edge\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is it clear what workflow this is and that it is in a start state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"First visible text is the clipped fragment 'cycle.' above 'Share why this title belongs on the ballot'\",\n          \"why\": \"The workflow is inferable from the chips and 'Submit nomination', but the clipped hero withholds the book identity that would make the start state concrete.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is it clear why the disabled action is disabled?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Not available' pill beside 'Another community role manages this item.'\",\n          \"why\": \"No role is named and no path is offered, so the user cannot act on or understand the restriction.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"fdb882b44de6ae8dffed1de692bbd1564b51788df72ba0bb847c16d0f8fc6e28\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The strongest of the nomination screens: the app bar reads 'Book nomination', the hero says 'Nominate Parable of the Sower' with the subtitle 'Parable of the Sower by Octavia E. Butler', and 'Nomination details' carries a genuinely product-specific line — 'The nomination will be visible to members for the February vote and tied to the discussion meeting.' Two defects: the same secondary action is rendered twice ('Edit nomination' as an outlined button in the grey band and again as a dark-green ghost link at the bottom-right of the 'Nomination details' card, where the green-on-dark-grey rendering is close to unreadable), and the chip row ('Book title entered', 'Author confirmed') labels the completion of fields rather than showing their values, which is redundant when the title and author are already printed two lines above.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"One nomination form sheet showing the entered title, author, and rationale as values, with a single unambiguous secondary 'Edit' affordance at readable contrast.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"App bar 'Book nomination' with X close\", \"'Nominate Parable of the Sower' hero over 'Parable of the Sower by Octavia E. Butler'\", \"'The nomination will be visible to members for the February vote and tied to the discussion meeting.'\", \"Filled teal 'Submit nomination' CTA\", \"Duplicate 'Edit nomination' rendered as low-contrast green text bottom-right\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the copy describe actual community content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Parable of the Sower by Octavia E. Butler' and 'visible to members for the February vote'\",\n          \"why\": \"Real title, real author, real cycle — this reads as product copy, not placeholder.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are the actions clear?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Submit nomination' filled teal button plus two separate 'Edit nomination' controls\",\n          \"why\": \"The primary is clear; the duplicated secondary, one of which is barely visible, is the flaw.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"ab24edb901bd56c7372840edf7e241af6db0c7b68a7ce0712c8be735935d8843\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Completion is legible — the subtitle 'Octavia E. Butler - February reading cycle.' and the confirmation strip 'Nomination submitted' read correctly — but the sentence 'Parable of the Sower is on the February ballot with title, author, rationale, and meeting context.' is printed twice in full (hero body and again inside 'Ballot record') and starts a third time in the clipped 'Nomination submitted' banner at the bottom. 'Edit nomination' likewise appears twice. The screen also still carries the pre-save instructional line 'This view shows editable details, current progress, and the next step before saving.' even though the nomination has already been submitted, which contradicts the completed state.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A submitted-nomination receipt stating the outcome once, with post-submission affordances only (withdraw/edit) and no pre-save instructional text.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'Nominate Parable of the Sower' hero\", \"'Ballot record' card repeating the hero sentence verbatim\", \"Clipped 'Nomination submitted' banner behind the bottom nav\", \"'This view shows editable details… before saving.' still present after submission\", \"'Edit nomination' shown twice\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the complete state unambiguous?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Nomination submitted' banner plus 'Ballot record' card\",\n          \"why\": \"Yes — but the retained 'before saving' instructional copy muddies it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is there thin or repeated content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Parable of the Sower is on the February ballot with title, author, rationale, and meeting context.' appears twice in full\",\n          \"why\": \"The same sentence stacked in consecutive cards reads as template duplication rather than layered detail.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"68b491f904731e1e1d566371503d623d73862fa30d5c34d01001179d8a145cec\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-selection-publish-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-selection-publish-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"A clean start state: 'Publish February selection' with the causal subtitle 'Parable of the Sower won the member vote.' and four concrete delivery chips — 'Audience: members', 'From organizer', 'Today 5:00 PM', 'Inbox + push' — that answer who/when/where before the 'Publish announcement' CTA. Weaknesses are below the fold: the 'Upcoming events' section header 'Dates, capacity, and attendance actions.' is a thin generic band with no content of its own, and the 'Meeting event RSVP' card underneath truncates to 'Waiting for the organizer to publish the event upda…' while its own action row is cut off by the bottom nav, so the reader cannot see what that card offers.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"Publish-start with the announcement draft body visible alongside the delivery chips, and supporting event cards that show real dates rather than a truncated waiting message.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'Publish February selection' hero with megaphone icon\", \"'Parable of the Sower won the member vote.'\", \"Chips: 'Audience: members', 'From organizer', 'Today 5:00 PM', 'Inbox + push'\", \"'Upcoming events — Dates, capacity, and attendance actions.' content-free band\", \"'Waiting for the organizer to publish the event upda…' truncated\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the workflow and its start state clear?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Publish February selection' with an unpressed 'Publish announcement' ghost CTA\",\n          \"why\": \"The announcement has plainly not gone out yet; the state reads correctly.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is any content thin?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Upcoming events / Dates, capacity, and attendance actions.'\",\n          \"why\": \"The band is a label with no events in it, occupying a full card's height.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"6af7a24a92f0b9567e53f79051f81d74903681c1556ad56846c64e8ac2f7c16e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-selection-publish-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-selection-publish-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The 'Selection announcement' sheet is well composed: hero 'Publish February selection' / 'February book: Parable of the Sower', a clear pre-send explanation ('Preview the announcement body, sender, audience, delivery time, and member inbox preview before publishing.'), and 'Announcement publish details' telling the organizer exactly what recipients get — 'Members will receive the selected book, meeting date, and discussion prompt in their inbox.' The gap is that the screen promises a preview and a message body it never shows in frame: the 'Announcement preview' card is only a clipped heading at the very bottom, so the organizer is asked to press a filled 'Publish announcement' button without the actual text visible. 'Save draft' is again duplicated as a button and a near-invisible teal ghost link bottom-right.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A publish confirmation sheet where the announcement body itself is visible above the Publish button, not below the fold.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"App bar 'Selection announcement'\", \"'February book: Parable of the Sower'\", \"'Members will receive the selected book, meeting date, and discussion prompt in their inbox.'\", \"Filled teal 'Publish announcement' CTA\", \"'Announcement preview' heading clipped at the bottom edge\", \"Duplicate 'Save draft' as low-contrast teal text\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Can the user tell what will be sent before publishing?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Preview the announcement body, sender, audience, delivery time, and member inbox preview before publishing.'\",\n          \"why\": \"The copy promises a body preview but the body is not on screen — only the metadata chips are.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the copy specific to this club?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'February book: Parable of the Sower'\",\n          \"why\": \"Yes; it names the actual selection and cycle.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"020ea4a7b06381ad49d08b125ec447fc9ac74ce647dc1724e7e70519f1288524\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-selection-publish-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-selection-publish-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This screen contradicts itself. The hero says 'Members received the February selection announcement with book, sender, timing, and next steps.' and the bottom strip reads 'Selection published' — yet the card between them still shows the pre-publish instructional line 'Message body, audience, delivery timing, preview, and draft option stay visible before publishing.' with an active 'Save draft' button, and 'Member inbox result' offers a second 'Save draft'. Offering to draft an announcement that has already been delivered is a wrong-state action, not a cosmetic issue. The delivered sentence is also printed twice in full and a third time in the clipped banner, and 'Today 5:00 PM' remains phrased as a future delivery slot after delivery.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A published-announcement receipt showing delivery timestamp and reach, with draft controls removed and post-send actions (view in inbox, resend) in their place.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'Members received the February selection announcement…' in the hero\", \"'…stay visible before publishing.' retained after publishing\", \"Two separate 'Save draft' buttons post-publish\", \"'Member inbox result' repeating the hero sentence verbatim\", \"Clipped 'Selection published' banner behind the nav\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Do the visible actions make sense for the completed state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Save draft' buttons shown alongside 'Members received the February selection announcement'\",\n          \"why\": \"A draft action after delivery is contradictory and would mislead an organizer about whether the send happened.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is content repeated?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Members received the February selection announcement with book, sender, timing, and next steps.' appears twice in full\",\n          \"why\": \"Consecutive cards restate the identical sentence with no added information.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"ef5759c7f3eb3728d4817c0ebbe4c97f7fc428c3d7c4c839eba061c988e47c88\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The row is labelled reading-material, but the in-focus teal card is 'Shared library item / Borrow and manage the club library item.' — a different workflow — and the actual 'Reading material' card sits minimized below with body text from an advertising product: 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…' and a button reading 'Open ad details'. A neighborhood book club has no ad preferences; this is content leaked from another surface. The in-focus card is itself contentless: no book, no chapter, no guide name, only harness chips 'Details ready', 'Editable', 'State saved' and a CTA phrased as a verb-plus-component-name, 'Start shared library item'. A debug affordance, 'In-focus product surface … Expand', is visible above the card.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A reading-material start card naming the current guide (e.g. the Parable of the Sower chapter guide), what it contains, and an 'Open reading guide' action — with no ad-preference copy anywhere.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'In-focus product surface' / 'Expand' debug strip\", \"Teal hero is 'Shared library item', not reading material\", \"'Reading material' card body reads 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…'\", \"'Open ad details' button\", \"Chips 'Details ready', 'Editable', 'State saved'\", \"CTA 'Start shared library item'\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the copy describe actual book club content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…' with 'Open ad details'\",\n          \"why\": \"Advertising-preference copy has no place in a book club's reading material and reads as content from an unrelated product.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the workflow identifiable?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The focused card is titled 'Shared library item', not 'Reading material'\",\n          \"why\": \"The screen foregrounds a different workflow than the row it is evidencing.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"25bd94bc3a4d4206dc8aba20efd34abfa4c44f15ff229d6cf313e1ac788075c2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The app bar and hero finally say 'Reading material' with a plausible subtitle, 'Current reading guides and author links are available.' — but everything beneath it is scaffolding. The section is headed 'Task details', its entire body is the one-line restatement 'Open the current reading guide.', the chips are 'Details ready' / 'Editable' / 'State saved', and the filled teal primary CTA reads 'Open ad details' — an advertising action on a reading-guide sheet. No guide title, chapter range, author link, or page is shown, so a member could not tell what they are about to open. A further 'Activity details' card is clipped at the bottom with its content cut off, and 'Edit details' is duplicated as a faint teal ghost link.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A reading-guide sheet listing the actual guide entries — chapter ranges, author links, discussion prompts — with an 'Open reading guide' primary action.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"App bar 'Reading material'\", \"'Current reading guides and author links are available.'\", \"Section titled 'Task details' with body 'Open the current reading guide.'\", \"Filled teal CTA 'Open ad details'\", \"Chips 'Details ready', 'Editable', 'State saved'\", \"'Activity details' card clipped at bottom\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the primary action match the workflow?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Filled teal button 'Open ad details' under the heading 'Reading material'\",\n          \"why\": \"The main action names an ad surface, so the screen's single most prominent control contradicts its own title.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is real content shown where content is expected?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Task details' card contains only 'Open the current reading guide.'\",\n          \"why\": \"The detail card restates the CTA instead of listing any guide, leaving the card visually thin.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"1e98b5ba316a3b397a47dbcadc3849afa88a018a1f4f3ca386ece4cc617bdc6b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The completion payload is the four-word sentence 'Reading material opened.', printed twice — once under 'Saved details' and again in the 'Saved' strip — plus a 'Saved' check pill. Nothing identifies which guide was opened, for which book or chapter, or when. The screen also still shows the pre-save instructional band 'This view shows editable details, current progress, and the next step before saving.' with an 'Edit response' button after the save has completed. Below the card roughly a third of the viewport is empty dark-green background broken only by a collapsed 'Local package details' disclosure row, so the completed state reads as an unfinished page rather than a receipt.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A completed reading-material state naming the opened guide and its book/chapter with a timestamp, and filling the viewport with the guide's contents or next steps.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'Saved details — Reading material opened.'\", \"'Saved' strip repeating 'Reading material opened.'\", \"'Saved' check pill\", \"'…before saving.' instructional band retained post-save\", \"Large empty region above the bottom nav\", \"Collapsed 'Local package details' row\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Can the user tell what was completed?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Reading material opened.' with no guide, book, or chapter named\",\n          \"why\": \"The state is legible but the object of the action is entirely unidentified.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the layout production-grade?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Roughly a third of the screen below 'Local package details' is bare background\",\n          \"why\": \"A completed screen with a large empty band and a four-word payload reads as scaffolding.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"518edf9cc7e2861b531c6c6d6e09d746d3177fced2c749e9a22f03dc45d2cd98\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The ballot chips are excellent and specific — '3 nominations', 'Closes Jan 20', '1 member vote', 'Leading title' — and 'Record vote' is an unambiguous CTA. But the periwinkle hero is clipped mid-sentence at the top ('Parable of the Sower is leading the / ballot for the next monthly discussion.'), so the ballot's own title never appears in frame. Below, two dark cards ('Shared library item' and 'Reading material') are byte-identical shells: same icon, same 'Minimized' pill, same 'Another community role manages this item.' line, same 'Tap for expanded view' / 'Member form' / 'Expand' / 'Not available' control grid — a visibly repeated generic card shell with an unexplained disabled action in each. The 'Library' nav pill is clipped at the right edge.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A vote start card showing the ballot name and all three nominated titles with their current counts, and supporting cards carrying distinct real content instead of duplicate shells.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Clipped hero line 'Parable of the Sower is leading the'\", \"Chips '3 nominations', 'Closes Jan 20', '1 member vote', 'Leading title'\", \"'Record vote' ghost CTA\", \"Two identical dark cards both reading 'Another community role manages this item.'\", \"Two 'Not available' disabled pills\", \"'Library' nav pill clipped\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the ballot legible as a start state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'1 member vote' and 'Closes Jan 20' with an unpressed 'Record vote'\",\n          \"why\": \"State reads as pre-vote correctly, but the clipped hero withholds the ballot's identity.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are there repeated generic card shells?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Shared library item' and 'Reading material' cards share identical layout and the identical sentence 'Another community role manages this item.'\",\n          \"why\": \"Two stacked cards differing only by title is the textbook repeated-shell failure.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"918ef3feeb3c83a03e7f42b7bd4b1182bc5faadd67cf1f362511462afe1f3e5f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The best-argued sheet in the set: app bar 'Cast book vote', hero 'February book ballot / February selection ballot', and a 'Ballot choice' card that states the voting rule in plain member-facing language — 'Your vote will count once for Parable of the Sower and can be changed before the ballot closes.' — directly above the filled teal 'Record vote' button, with 'Closes Jan 20' visible as the deadline. Two flaws: the sheet claims 'Compare nominated books, confirm your vote…' but only one of the three nominations is named anywhere in frame ('Ballot options' is a clipped heading at the very bottom), so no comparison is actually possible on screen; and 'Change vote' is duplicated as an outlined button and a dark-teal ghost link at low contrast.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A ballot sheet listing all three nominated titles with authors and current counts so the member can compare before recording a vote.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"App bar 'Cast book vote'\", \"'February book ballot' / 'February selection ballot'\", \"'Your vote will count once for Parable of the Sower and can be changed before the ballot closes.'\", \"Filled teal 'Record vote'\", \"'Ballot options' heading clipped at bottom edge\", \"Duplicate 'Change vote' as faint teal text\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the action and its consequence clear?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Your vote will count once for Parable of the Sower and can be changed before the ballot closes.'\",\n          \"why\": \"Both the effect and the reversibility window are stated next to the button — genuinely good product copy.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the screen deliver what it promises?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Compare nominated books' but only one title appears; 'Ballot options' is clipped\",\n          \"why\": \"The comparison the copy offers is not visible on the screen.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"e32a11ee741f0148d6dc064d83b5d0f5c12661bbc255e4ca38795547c226fb59\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Confirmation is clear — 'Vote saved' and a clipped 'Vote confirmed' strip, with the honest subtitle 'Vote between three member nominations.' and retained chips '3 nominations', 'Closes Jan 20', '1 member vote'. The defect is triplication: 'Your vote for Parable of the Sower is confirmed, status is saved, and it can be changed before the ballot closes.' appears three times on one scroll — hero body, 'Vote saved' card, and 'Vote confirmed' strip — and 'Change vote' appears twice. The '1 member vote' chip is also unchanged from the start screen even though a vote has just been recorded, which undercuts the completed state. The pre-save band '…the next step before saving.' is still present after saving.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A vote receipt stating the confirmed choice once, with the tally chip incremented to reflect the vote just cast and a single 'Change vote' affordance.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'February book ballot' hero\", \"The confirmation sentence printed three times\", \"'1 member vote' chip unchanged after voting\", \"'Vote saved' and 'Vote confirmed' cards\", \"'Change vote' shown twice\", \"'…before saving.' band retained\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the complete state unambiguous?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Vote saved' heading and 'Vote confirmed' strip\",\n          \"why\": \"Yes — the state itself is unmistakable.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the data reflect the completed action?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'1 member vote' identical to the start screen's chip\",\n          \"why\": \"After recording a vote the tally should move; an unchanged count suggests the confirmation is decorative.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"a5e34536c2e5a54104cf4fa36428c9201399536bd8b912706ead61b7203ce600\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-search-ai-digest-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-search-ai-digest-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Content here is the most convincingly 'real' in the whole set: a member-plausible query, 'What should we discuss before chapter 6?', an answer summary that could only come from this book — 'Focus the chapter 6 discussion on mutual aid, scarcity, and Lauren's journal voice.' — and provenance framed as 'Cites member notes, the February nomination rationale, and the March discussion prompt.' The problems are structural rather than editorial: the citations are described ('Each citation shows source title, author or member, and why it is visible to this member.') but no actual citation list is rendered, so the user sees a promise instead of sources; the 'Ask follow-up' button is sliced in half by the bottom nav; and the debug strip 'In-focus product surface / Expand' sits above the content.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A digest start showing the query with an enumerated, tappable citation list rather than a prose description of what citations would contain.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Query: 'What should we discuss before chapter 6?'\", \"'Focus the chapter 6 discussion on mutual aid, scarcity, and Lauren's journal voice.'\", \"'Cites member notes, the February nomination rationale, and the March discussion prompt.'\", \"'Each citation shows source title, author or member, and why it is visible to this member.'\", \"'Ask follow-up' button clipped by the bottom nav\", \"'In-focus product surface' debug strip\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the content read as real book club material?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'mutual aid, scarcity, and Lauren's journal voice'\",\n          \"why\": \"These are specific to Parable of the Sower and could not be template text.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are the cited sources actually shown?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Citation detail — Each citation shows source title, author or member…'\",\n          \"why\": \"The screen describes the citation format instead of listing any citation.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"dea065f91186cdabfc0a02a16bca4ee50bb750128390207bf2833baea936585b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-search-ai-digest-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-search-ai-digest-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This sheet renders the same four-bullet block twice on one screen: 'Answer summary / Focus the chapter 6 discussion on mutual aid, scarcity, and Lauren's journal voice.', 'Source snippets / Cites member notes…' and 'Citation detail' appear inside the top 'Answer with sources' card and are then repeated verbatim inside the 'Answer actions' card below. Worse, the card titled 'Answer actions' — which announces 'Open cited sources, save the answer, refine the query, or share it with members.' — contains no tappable controls whatsoever, only prose bullets like 'Query and answer — The user sees the query, answer, citations, source visibility, and follow-up options.' That bullet is written about the user in third person, which is spec language rather than product copy, and the action sheet consequently offers no action.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"An answer sheet with real controls — Open source, Save to digest, Refine query, Share — and each source rendered once as a tappable citation row.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"App bar 'Reading guide answer'\", \"The 'Answer summary'/'Source snippets'/'Citation detail' block duplicated on one screen\", \"'Answer actions' card with no buttons\", \"'The user sees the query, answer, citations, source visibility, and follow-up options.' written in third person\", \"'Saved citation state — Save, share, refine, and stale-source handling are visible after opening the result.'\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are the available actions clear?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Answer actions — Open cited sources, save the answer, refine the query, or share it with members.' with no controls beneath it\",\n          \"why\": \"A card named for actions that renders none leaves the user with nothing to press.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the copy sound like product copy?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'The user sees the query, answer, citations, source visibility, and follow-up options.'\",\n          \"why\": \"Describing 'the user' in third person is requirements text surfaced into the UI.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"7f7ef22f005dba6bb077ac33f519833639971a5f414d83a202e2cc97c15cb539\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-search-ai-digest-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-search-ai-digest-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The completion marker works well visually — a periwinkle 'Guide saved' banner reading 'The reading guide now shows query, answer, citations, source visibility, save state, and follow-up prompts.' stands out against the teal page and clearly signals the saved state. But it is again a description of what the guide contains rather than the guide itself: above it the identical 'Answer with sources' block from the start screen is re-shown unchanged, and the 'Saved answer' card below is clipped to a single cut-off line behind the bottom nav. There is no visible timestamp, no digest location, and no 'View digest' action, so a member cannot get to the thing that was just saved.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A saved-digest confirmation with a timestamp and a direct 'View in club digest' link, showing the saved answer rather than restating the pre-save card.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Periwinkle 'Guide saved' banner against the teal page\", \"'The reading guide now shows query, answer, citations, source visibility, save state, and follow-up prompts.'\", \"'Answer with sources' block unchanged from the start screen\", \"'Saved answer' card clipped to one cut-off line\", \"No timestamp or navigation to the digest\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the saved state legible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Guide saved' banner in contrasting periwinkle\",\n          \"why\": \"The colour break plus the heading make the completion unmistakable at a glance.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Can the user reach what was saved?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"No 'View digest' control anywhere; 'Saved answer' is clipped\",\n          \"why\": \"The completion is announced but not navigable.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"4cd2f815d16f0b94c2fb2339427d65fef3a83122a55a3487589d5171389ad2fb\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-meeting-rsvp-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-meeting-rsvp-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This is captured on the wrong surface for an RSVP start state. Nearly the whole viewport is the knowledge/search workflow — a teal 'Knowledge and search / Cited answers, source visibility, and saved digests.' band, then the 'Answer with sources' card with the chapter-6 query, then 'Reading guide answer' — while the RSVP card itself is reduced to a sliced button row, 'Expand | RSVP to event', jammed against the app bar with its title and event details scrolled out of view. A member landing here cannot see the meeting date, venue, capacity, or their current response; the only RSVP evidence is a half-cut button. The 'Library' nav pill is also clipped at the right edge, and the debug strip 'In-focus product surface / Expand' is visible.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The RSVP card in full frame at start: 'Parable discussion night', Thu Feb 15, 7:00 PM, Maya's living room, 10 of 14 spots, with Going/Maybe/Not going not yet chosen.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Clipped 'Expand | RSVP to event' row at the top edge\", \"'Knowledge and search — Cited answers, source visibility, and saved digests.' occupying the upper third\", \"Full 'Answer with sources' card with the chapter-6 query\", \"'Reading guide answer' heading clipped at the bottom\", \"'Library' nav pill clipped at right edge\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is it clear this is the RSVP workflow in its start state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Only the half-cut text 'RSVP to event' relates to RSVP; the rest is the reading-guide surface\",\n          \"why\": \"The evidenced workflow is not the workflow shown, so the start state cannot be judged from this screen.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is any event detail visible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"No date, time, venue or capacity appears anywhere in frame\",\n          \"why\": \"The RSVP decision inputs are entirely off-screen.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"0c473b2461e0d45fe1ff41e973cf8adeedb28a0f19a14b8df99e1ddc468bf69d\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-meeting-rsvp-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-meeting-rsvp-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The strongest screen reviewed. The blue sheet is titled 'Book meeting RSVP', names the event 'Parable discussion night' with the subtitle 'Parable of the Sower discussion', and the 'Choose attendance' card gives four concrete data chips — 'Thu, Feb 15', '7:00 PM', 'Maya's living room', '10 of 14 spots' — plus a genuinely useful explanation of the semantics: 'Going reserves a seat and sends a reminder. Maybe keeps the meeting on your calendar without taking capacity.' The one real gap is that the copy above says 'Going/Maybe/Not going options are visible' but only a single filled 'RSVP to event' button is rendered — the three response options are not actually selectable on screen — and 'Change response' is duplicated as a low-contrast ghost link.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"An RSVP sheet with three distinct Going / Maybe / Not going controls rather than one generic 'RSVP to event' button.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"App bar 'Book meeting RSVP'\", \"'Parable discussion night' / 'Parable of the Sower discussion'\", \"Chips 'Thu, Feb 15', '7:00 PM', 'Maya's living room', '10 of 14 spots'\", \"'Going reserves a seat and sends a reminder. Maybe keeps the meeting on your calendar without taking capacity.'\", \"Single filled 'RSVP to event' button despite three options being described\", \"Duplicate 'Change response' as faint text\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the copy describe real community content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Maya's living room' and '10 of 14 spots'\",\n          \"why\": \"A named host venue and a real capacity ratio are unmistakably product content, not placeholder.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Do the described options match the rendered controls?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Going/Maybe/Not going options are visible' above a single 'RSVP to event' button\",\n          \"why\": \"The three options the copy promises are not present as controls.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"d14f70288a77ea3ad86cd790291f75f234511f7a024b90eed9c7dbe22284d7cc\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-meeting-rsvp-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-meeting-rsvp-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Good completion: the subtitle 'Thu, Feb 15 at 7:00 PM - Maya's living room.' restates the commitment in one line and 'RSVP confirmed' closes it out, with all four chips retained. The recurring template flaw applies — 'You are going to the Parable discussion; seat count, reminder, and change response stay visible.' is printed three times (hero, 'Response options', 'RSVP confirmed') and 'Change response' twice. The capacity chip still reads '10 of 14 spots', unchanged from before the RSVP, so the seat the copy says was reserved is not reflected in the count. The 'RSVP confirmed' strip is clipped mid-sentence by the bottom nav.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"An RSVP receipt showing the chosen response as a state (e.g. 'Going'), an incremented seat count, and one change affordance.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'Thu, Feb 15 at 7:00 PM - Maya's living room.'\", \"'You are going to the Parable discussion…' printed three times\", \"'10 of 14 spots' unchanged after RSVP\", \"'Response options' card restating the hero\", \"'RSVP confirmed' strip clipped by the nav\", \"'Change response' shown twice\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completed state legible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'You are going to the Parable discussion' plus the 'RSVP confirmed' heading\",\n          \"why\": \"The user's own commitment is stated plainly in second person.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does displayed data reflect the completion?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'10 of 14 spots' identical to the pre-RSVP action screen\",\n          \"why\": \"A confirmed Going should consume a seat; the static count contradicts 'Going reserves a seat'.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"8e0ab70e21a2ed9c13b5eb987a1a9b9df0c72edbe2d267e8dd3e9a49d4ef4bd7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"No export surface appears on this screen at all. The frame is dominated by a purple 'Discussion thread' card — 'Prompt: What does community care require?' with chips 'From Jordan', 'Members only', '3 unread', 'Club scoped' — under a 'Messages and connections' band, followed by a 'Member tools / Useful actions for this community.' band. The export workflow's start state is therefore entirely unevidenced: no scope selection, no redaction choice, no destination, no 'Generate export' control. The card at the very top is clipped to two empty button outlines with no labels, and the 'Discussion thread' card's only status is a 'Waiting' pill with no explanation of what it is waiting on.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"An export start card naming the club export package, the record types in scope, redaction defaults, destination, and an enabled 'Generate export' action.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'Messages and connections — Member communication and relationship controls.'\", \"'Discussion thread / Prompt: What does community care require?' as the in-focus card\", \"Chips 'From Jordan', 'Members only', '3 unread', 'Club scoped'\", \"Unexplained 'Waiting' pill\", \"'Member tools / Useful actions for this community.' generic band\", \"Two label-less clipped button outlines at the top edge\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the export workflow visible in its start state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The focused purple card reads 'Discussion thread', and the words export, scope, redaction and checksum appear nowhere\",\n          \"why\": \"The screen shows a different workflow entirely, so it cannot evidence the export start state.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the 'Waiting' status explained?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Waiting' pill with no adjacent explanatory text\",\n          \"why\": \"A bare waiting state with no subject or expected duration is unactionable.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"1aec7237a9bacdbaedd9318145b3894f6c7a0dc303bea61ad50bfa238fcc0b69\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Content quality here is high and specific to a book club: a numbered five-step list — 'Reading data / Nominations, selected books, ballot counts, reading schedule, and meeting RSVP records.', 'Redaction preview / Member email, phone, and private thread metadata are redacted unless the owner has consent.', 'Checksum and audit / Checksum BC-042 and export timestamp are written to the owner audit history.', 'Download', and 'Rollback' — reads as real privacy-aware product copy, and the slate app bar 'Book club export package' distinguishes the surface from the teal community chrome. The weakness is that this action screen shows no action: no scope toggles, no redaction switches, no 'Generate export' button is in frame, and the 'Export workspace' card below merely describes what is visible ('Scope, redaction, checksum, destination, transfer status, rollback, and audit evidence are visible.') rather than rendering it.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"An export sheet where the described scope and redaction choices are actual controls, with a 'Generate export' primary button in frame.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Slate app bar 'Book club export package'\", \"Numbered steps 1–5 with distinct icons\", \"'Checksum BC-042 and export timestamp are written to the owner audit history.'\", \"'Change scope or cancel before export generation; previous exports stay in audit history.'\", \"'Export workspace' card describing controls rather than showing them\", \"No primary CTA visible in frame\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the copy real and specific?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Nominations, selected books, ballot counts, reading schedule, and meeting RSVP records.'\",\n          \"why\": \"It enumerates this club's actual record types rather than generic 'your data'.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Can the user act from this screen?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Scope, redaction, checksum, destination… are visible.' with no toggles or buttons rendered\",\n          \"why\": \"The action state describes affordances instead of presenting them.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"e217ad3a30563c5d1c14ee86b4b7fcca5a6a143141634fe41838a6d06897d145\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The completion reads acceptably: the page heading 'Book club export package' with 'Nominations, votes, RSVPs, threads, and reading schedule.' summarises the payload, and a slate 'Book archive generated' strip signals the result. But that strip is clipped to its title and one cut-off line by the bottom nav, so the archive's file size, timestamp, checksum result, and download control are all off-screen — the completed state's most important payload is exactly what is hidden. Above it the identical five-step list from the action screen is re-rendered unchanged, meaning most of the completed screen is a verbatim repeat of the prior state with nothing marked as done: none of the steps 1–5 show a completed indicator.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A generated-archive receipt with file name, size, timestamp, checksum verified state and a Download button in frame, with completed steps visibly checked off.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Heading 'Book club export package' with 'Nominations, votes, RSVPs, threads, and reading schedule.'\", \"Steps 1–5 repeated verbatim from the action screen with no completion marks\", \"'Book archive generated' strip clipped to one cut-off line\", \"No download control or file details visible\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completed state distinguishable from the action state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The same five numbered steps appear on both screens with no step marked complete\",\n          \"why\": \"Only the clipped 'Book archive generated' strip distinguishes them, and it is mostly hidden.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the export result actionable?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"No download button or file details visible in frame\",\n          \"why\": \"The owner cannot retrieve the archive the screen says was generated.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"14875014e3378dd9ec3194dbb350eb8b05f09eaf0cd1710262e258c04bf40006\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-discussion-message-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-discussion-message-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The purple thread card is sliced across its top — the first visible line is the half-cut 'Reply to the Parable discussion with a note scoped to club members.' — so the thread's title and prompt are scrolled out and only the chips 'From Jordan', 'Members only', '3 unread', 'Club scoped' plus a 'Send message' CTA survive. Below, a 'Member tools / Useful actions for this community.' band introduces two more identical dark shells ('Book nomination' and 'Book vote') that share the same truncated description 'Member form captures labeled details, privacy c…' and the same 'Tap for expanded view / Member form / Expand' control grid, so the lower half of the screen is duplicated chrome. The 'Library' nav pill is clipped at the right edge.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A discussion start showing the thread title, prompt, and the most recent member replies in full frame, with distinct supporting cards.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Clipped opening line 'Reply to the Parable discussion with a note scoped to club members.'\", \"Chips 'From Jordan', 'Members only', '3 unread', 'Club scoped'\", \"'Send message' ghost CTA\", \"'Member tools / Useful actions for this community.' generic band\", \"'Book nomination' and 'Book vote' cards sharing the truncated string 'Member form captures labeled details, privacy c…'\", \"'Library' nav pill clipped\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the thread identifiable at the start state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The thread title and prompt are scrolled off; only a clipped body line is visible\",\n          \"why\": \"'3 unread' implies replies exist, but none are shown and the subject is not named on screen.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the content below distinct?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Two cards both reading 'Member form captures labeled details, privacy c…'\",\n          \"why\": \"Identical truncated descriptions in stacked cards are repeated generic shells.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"5cf04447f6d8a27ad3681a0cba759c0f77134aa1bf4024f26a4e92e943607bbc\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-discussion-message-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-discussion-message-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"A well-scoped reply sheet: app bar 'Reply to discussion', hero 'Discussion thread / Parable discussion thread', and a 'Message delivery' card that states the privacy consequence directly above the send button — 'Your reply will appear in the club thread and stay scoped to current members.' — reinforced by the 'Members only' and 'Club scoped' chips. Two issues: there is no composer, no message field and no draft text anywhere, yet the primary control is a filled teal 'Send message', so it is unclear what would be sent; and the grey band above lists a large undifferentiated option set — 'Sender, recipient, message body, timestamp, reply, send, accept, decline, mute, archive, and block options are visible.' — while rendering only 'Archive thread', duplicated again as a faint ghost link bottom-right.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A reply sheet with a visible composer field and the prior thread messages above it, and only the moderation actions that are actually offered.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"App bar 'Reply to discussion'\", \"'Parable discussion thread'\", \"'Your reply will appear in the club thread and stay scoped to current members.'\", \"Filled teal 'Send message' with no composer field on screen\", \"'Sender, recipient, message body, timestamp, reply, send, accept, decline, mute, archive, and block options are visible.'\", \"Duplicate 'Archive thread' as low-contrast text\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the privacy scope clear?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'stay scoped to current members' with 'Members only' and 'Club scoped' chips\",\n          \"why\": \"Audience is stated in both copy and chips right next to the send action.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Can the user tell what will be sent?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"No message composer or draft body is visible above 'Send message'\",\n          \"why\": \"A send action with no visible content is not safely actionable.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"e90705523609677dfe743cbf0492701f919a4923603c0c1dddb70d9e1b2f0680\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-discussion-message-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-discussion-message-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Completion is legible — 'Prompt: What does community care require?' anchors the thread and 'Reply sent' closes the loop — but the confirmation sentence 'Your discussion message is posted to the Parable thread with sender and member scope.' is printed three times (hero, 'Conversation record', 'Reply sent'), and 'Archive thread' appears twice. Critically, the reply that was just posted is nowhere on screen: there is no message text, no author, no timestamp, only assertions that a message exists. The '3 unread' chip is also unchanged from before sending, and the option-inventory line 'Sender, recipient, message body, timestamp, reply, send, accept, decline, mute, archive, and block options are visible.' is retained despite most of those controls not being rendered.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A posted-reply state showing the actual message text with its author and timestamp in the thread, stated once.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'Prompt: What does community care require?'\", \"Confirmation sentence printed three times\", \"'Conversation record' card restating the hero\", \"'Reply sent' strip clipped by the bottom nav\", \"'3 unread' unchanged after posting\", \"'Archive thread' shown twice\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the sent state clear?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Reply sent' heading and 'Your discussion message is posted to the Parable thread'\",\n          \"why\": \"The completion itself is unambiguous.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the posted content shown?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"No message body, author, or timestamp appears anywhere on the screen\",\n          \"why\": \"The thread claims a post exists but never renders it, leaving the card thin.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"5e824d3fb1cd38e34332e0e13dad5a1317a0a0d1b3fa47b549ba81d640927deb\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The library item is never identified: the teal card is clipped at the top to '…and claim shared items.' and carries only harness chips 'Details ready', 'Editable', 'State saved' with a CTA phrased as a component name, 'Start shared library item' — no book, no copy count, no borrower, no due date. Directly below, the 'Reading material' card again shows the out-of-domain string 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…' with an 'Open ad details' button inside a book club. Below that, roughly the bottom third of the viewport is bare dark-green background interrupted only by a collapsed 'Local package details' disclosure row, so the screen ends in empty space where a lending queue or item list should be.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A shared-library start naming the item (e.g. the club's copy of Parable of the Sower), who holds it, the queue, and a 'Borrow' or 'Join queue' action.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"Clipped top line '…and claim shared items.'\", \"Chips 'Details ready', 'Editable', 'State saved'\", \"CTA 'Start shared library item'\", \"'Reading material' card reading 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…' with 'Open ad details'\", \"Bottom third of screen empty dark-green background\", \"Collapsed 'Local package details' row\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Which library item is this?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"No item title, holder, or due date appears; only 'Start shared library item'\",\n          \"why\": \"The workflow's subject is entirely unnamed, so the start state describes a mechanism rather than a thing.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the visual layout production-grade?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"A large empty region between 'Local package details' and the bottom nav\",\n          \"why\": \"Substantial unfilled space where item content belongs reads as an incomplete screen.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"e216d02e58570192eca08e1ba31e96782523d4bd0ed539e56ad52c8dbb1d9c09\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The sheet is titled 'Shared library item' and its hero subtitle and body simply swap two generic sentences with each other — 'Members can borrow, queue for, return, and claim shared items.' as the subtitle and 'Borrow and manage the club library item.' as the body — then the 'Task details' card repeats 'Borrow and manage the club library item.' a third time. The three chips are framework states ('Details ready', 'Editable', 'State saved') rather than lending facts, and the filled teal primary CTA reads 'Start shared library item', which names a component rather than an action a member would take ('Borrow', 'Join queue', 'Return'). Nothing identifies the item, its holder, its queue position, or a due date. An 'Activity details' card is clipped at the bottom and 'Edit details' is duplicated as a faint teal link.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A lending sheet naming the item and its current custody — who has it, when it is due, how many are queued — with 'Borrow' / 'Join queue' / 'Return' as the actions.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"App bar 'Shared library item'\", \"Subtitle and body are two interchangeable generic sentences\", \"'Task details' repeating 'Borrow and manage the club library item.'\", \"Chips 'Details ready', 'Editable', 'State saved'\", \"Filled teal CTA 'Start shared library item'\", \"'Activity details' card clipped at the bottom\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the primary action meaningful?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Filled teal button 'Start shared library item'\",\n          \"why\": \"'Start' plus the component's own name is developer phrasing; a member borrows or queues, they do not 'start' an item.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the copy describe real content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Borrow and manage the club library item.' appearing three times with no item named\",\n          \"why\": \"Restating the same generic sentence in three slots is placeholder scaffolding.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"8d7a90e2c4e18d643f3e30dad59e2db4b16ada197c0af456255be2ec9c125a77\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The entire completion payload is one sentence, 'Shared library custody state updated.', printed three times — as the hero body, inside 'Saved details', and inside the 'Saved' strip — alongside a 'Saved' check pill. 'Custody state updated' is internal vocabulary, not member language, and it names neither the item, the previous holder, the new holder, nor a due date, so nothing on the screen tells a member what actually changed. The pre-save band 'This view shows editable details, current progress, and the next step before saving.' with its 'Edit response' button is still shown after saving, and the 'Reading material' card below is clipped mid-title behind the bottom nav.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A completed borrow/return receipt naming the item, the new holder, and the due date in member language, with a single confirmation.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"'Shared library custody state updated.' printed three times\", \"'Saved' check pill\", \"Chips 'Details ready', 'Editable', 'State saved' unchanged from the start state\", \"'…the next step before saving.' band retained after saving\", \"'Reading material' card clipped mid-title by the nav\"],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Can a member tell what changed?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Shared library custody state updated.' with no item, holder, or date\",\n          \"why\": \"The sentence is a system-level statement that conveys no borrowable fact to the member.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the copy member-facing?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The phrase 'custody state updated'\",\n          \"why\": \"This is internal data-model vocabulary rather than product language like 'You borrowed…' or 'Returned to the club shelf'.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"0dc23471ec00b00b9f6cc176c5294d0c2385cbf154ff0863d605a32464be3b4f\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"export-start-shows-discussion-thread\",\n      \"title\": \"Export-metadata start state shows the discussion thread, not the export surface\",\n      \"description\": \"The screen evidencing the export workflow's start state contains no export surface at all. The in-focus card is a purple 'Discussion thread' with 'Prompt: What does community care require?', chips 'From Jordan', 'Members only', '3 unread', 'Club scoped', and an unexplained 'Waiting' pill, under a 'Messages and connections' band. No scope selection, redaction option, destination, checksum, or generate action is visible. The meeting-RSVP start screen has the same defect in reverse — it is parked on the 'Knowledge and search' / 'Answer with sources' surface with only a sliced 'RSVP to event' button at the top edge.\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-meeting-rsvp-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Capture each start state with that workflow's own card scrolled fully into frame — the export package card with its scope/redaction/destination controls, and the RSVP card with 'Parable discussion night', Thu Feb 15, 7:00 PM, Maya's living room and 10 of 14 spots visible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"ad-copy-in-book-club-reading-material\",\n      \"title\": \"Advertising-preference copy and an 'Open ad details' CTA appear inside the reading-material workflow\",\n      \"description\": \"The 'Reading material' card renders body text from an advertising product — 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…' — with a button labelled 'Open ad details', on the reading-material start, the library-item start, and again as the filled teal primary CTA on the reading-material action sheet whose app bar reads 'Reading material'. A neighborhood book club has no ad preferences; this is content leaked in from an unrelated surface and it makes the most prominent control on the action screen contradict the screen's own title.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-action\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Replace the ad-preference copy and 'Open ad details' action with reading-guide content — the guide's book and chapter range, author links, discussion prompts — and an 'Open reading guide' primary action.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"library-and-reading-workflows-are-scaffolding\",\n      \"title\": \"Shared-library and reading-material workflows show framework scaffolding instead of club content\",\n      \"description\": \"Across all six screens of these two workflows the only content is generic: headings 'Task details', 'Saved details', 'Activity details'; chips 'Details ready', 'Editable', 'State saved'; a CTA that names its own component, 'Start shared library item'; and completion payloads of one sentence each — 'Reading material opened.' and 'Shared library custody state updated.' — the latter using internal data-model vocabulary. No item title, holder, queue position, due date, guide name, chapter, or timestamp appears anywhere. The library-item action sheet uses the same generic sentence in its subtitle, body, and Task details card.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-action\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-action\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Author real content for both workflows to the standard the vote and RSVP screens already meet: name the item and its custody ('Maya has the club copy until Feb 22, 2 members queued') and the guide and its scope, and replace 'Start shared library item' with 'Borrow', 'Join queue', or 'Return'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"complete-states-triplicate-confirmation\",\n      \"title\": \"Every complete state prints its confirmation sentence three times\",\n      \"description\": \"On each complete screen the same sentence appears as the hero body, again inside a record card, and a third time in the trailing confirmation strip. Examples: 'Your vote for Parable of the Sower is confirmed, status is saved, and it can be changed before the ballot closes.' (hero / 'Vote saved' / 'Vote confirmed'); 'You are going to the Parable discussion; seat count, reminder, and change response stay visible.' (hero / 'Response options' / 'RSVP confirmed'); 'Your discussion message is posted to the Parable thread with sender and member scope.' (hero / 'Conversation record' / 'Reply sent'). The secondary action is likewise duplicated ('Change vote', 'Change response', 'Archive thread', 'Edit nomination', 'Save draft'), with the second copy rendered as a low-contrast green ghost link at the card's bottom-right that is barely readable on the dark card.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-meeting-rsvp-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-discussion-message-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-selection-publish-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"State the outcome once and let subsequent cards add new information (timestamp, resulting record, next step). Render each secondary action once, at a contrast ratio readable against the card background.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"publish-complete-offers-save-draft\",\n      \"title\": \"Published announcement still offers 'Save draft' and pre-publish copy\",\n      \"description\": \"The selection-publish complete screen states 'Members received the February selection announcement with book, sender, timing, and next steps.' and shows a 'Selection published' strip, yet between them it retains the pre-send line 'Message body, audience, delivery timing, preview, and draft option stay visible before publishing.' with an active 'Save draft' button, and offers a second 'Save draft' inside 'Member inbox result'. 'Today 5:00 PM' also still reads as a scheduled future slot after delivery. Offering to draft an already-delivered announcement is a wrong-state action that could make an organizer doubt whether the send occurred.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-selection-publish-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Remove draft controls and pre-publish instructional copy from the published state; show delivery timestamp and reach, with post-send actions such as 'View in inbox' or 'Resend'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"top-clipping-and-nav-overflow\",\n      \"title\": \"Hero cards sliced mid-sentence at the top of frame and the 'Library' nav pill runs off the right edge\",\n      \"description\": \"Six screens open on a cut-off line rather than a card top: 'cycle.' on nomination start, 'Parable of the Sower is leading the' on vote start, 'Reply to the Parable discussion with a note scoped to club members.' on discussion start, 'and claim shared items.' on library start, 'Expand | RSVP to event' on RSVP start, and two label-less button outlines on export start. Separately, the bottom navigation row overflows horizontally so the 'Library' pill is cut by the right screen edge on nomination start, vote start, discussion start and RSVP start. Trailing confirmation strips ('Nomination submitted', 'Selection published', 'RSVP confirmed', 'Reply sent', 'Book archive generated', 'Saved answer') are also each clipped mid-sentence by the bottom nav.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-discussion-message-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-meeting-rsvp-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Anchor each capture so the focused card's title is fully visible below the app bar, add bottom padding so trailing confirmation strips clear the nav, and fix the bottom nav so all four tabs fit within the screen width.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"unexplained-not-available-and-repeated-shells\",\n      \"title\": \"Repeated generic card shells with unexplained 'Not available' actions\",\n      \"description\": \"Background cards repeat an identical shell — icon, 'Minimized' pill, 'Tap for expanded view', 'Member form', 'Expand', trailing action — differing only by title. On vote start, 'Shared library item' and 'Reading material' are visually identical and both read 'Another community role manages this item.' with a disabled 'Not available' pill that names no role and offers no path. On discussion start, 'Book nomination' and 'Book vote' both carry the same truncated description 'Member form captures labeled details, privacy c…'. A debug affordance, 'In-focus product surface … Expand', is also visible on three screens.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-discussion-message-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-start\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-search-ai-digest-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Give each background card its own real summary content, replace 'Not available' with a reason naming the responsible role and any available next step, and remove the 'In-focus product surface' debug strip from production surfaces.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"cards-describe-controls-instead-of-rendering-them\",\n      \"title\": \"Several cards describe affordances in prose rather than rendering them\",\n      \"description\": \"The AI-digest action sheet's 'Answer actions' card promises 'Open cited sources, save the answer, refine the query, or share it with members.' but contains no tappable controls, and one of its bullets is written about the user in third person: 'The user sees the query, answer, citations, source visibility, and follow-up options.' The same sheet duplicates the whole 'Answer summary / Source snippets / Citation detail' block twice on one screen. Similarly, the export action sheet says 'Scope, redaction, checksum, destination, transfer status, rollback, and audit evidence are visible' with no controls in frame; the RSVP sheet says 'Going/Maybe/Not going options are visible' but renders one generic 'RSVP to event' button; the discussion sheet lists eleven options ('reply, send, accept, decline, mute, archive, and block…') but renders only 'Archive thread'; and the publish sheet promises a body preview whose card is clipped off-screen.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-search-ai-digest-action\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-action\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-meeting-rsvp-action\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-discussion-message-action\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-selection-publish-action\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Render the described controls as real controls — distinct Going/Maybe/Not going options, citation rows that open sources, export scope and redaction toggles — and delete spec-voice bullets that narrate what 'the user sees'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"counts-unchanged-after-completion\",\n      \"title\": \"Counts and chips do not change between action and complete states\",\n      \"description\": \"The vote complete screen still shows '1 member vote' after the member records a vote, and the RSVP complete screen still shows '10 of 14 spots' after confirming Going, even though the action sheet stated 'Going reserves a seat and sends a reminder.' The discussion complete screen still shows '3 unread' after the reply is posted, and the export complete screen re-renders the same five numbered steps as the action screen with none marked done. The completion text asserts a change the visible data contradicts.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-meeting-rsvp-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-discussion-message-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-export-metadata-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Recompute chips and counters for the completed state — increment the vote tally and seat count, clear or decrement unread, and mark completed export steps — so the data corroborates the confirmation copy.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"internal-instructional-copy-in-ui\",\n      \"title\": \"Internal 'before saving' instructional text persists into saved and published states\",\n      \"description\": \"The string 'This view shows editable details, current progress, and the next step before saving.' appears verbatim on the nomination, vote, RSVP, reading-material and library-item screens, including on complete states where the save has already happened, paired with an 'Edit response' or 'Edit nomination' button. Chip labels like 'Details ready', 'Editable', 'State saved' and 'Book title entered' / 'Author confirmed' similarly report harness status rather than club data — the latter two are redundant when the title and author are printed two lines above them.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-vote-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-reading-material-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-library-item-complete\", \"neighborhood-book-club-book-nomination-action\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Remove the pre-save instructional band from completed states, and replace status-report chips with the values they refer to (the entered title, the confirmed author, the saved timestamp).\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":16002,"ttft_stream_ms":15110,"time_to_request_ms":14136,"type":"result","duration_ms":587151,"uuid":"76c95938-df74-41c0-9a36-4addeb6407e0"}
